      "predicate": "chuckled with glee along with",
      "target": "e4",
      "evidence": "<DW53> shook himself, and fairly chuckled with glee, as did also his two companions; but presently Miss Mary...\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e1",
      "predicate": "bade good-by to",
      "target": "e2",
      "evidence": "And then I bade him good-by, and begged him to come again;"
    },
    {
      "source": "e1",
      "predicate": "shook himself and chuckled with glee along with",
      "target": "e3",
      "evidence": "<DW53> shook himself, and fairly chuckled with glee, as did also his two companions; but presently Miss Mary...\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e2",
      "predicate": "said to",
      "target": "e1",
      "evidence": "\"<DW53>, you have saved my life, and perhaps the Madam's and Cracker's too. Give me your paw, and receive my warmest thanks for your timely aid.\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e2",
      "predicate": "added to",
      "target": "e1",
      "evidence": "\"We have not been the best of friends, lately,\" she added, \"but I trust all will be different now. And the next time you are invited to a party...\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e3",
      "predicate": "responded to",
      "target": "e2",
      "evidence": "\"And for my part, Miss Mary,\" responded the raccoon warmly, \"I beg you to consider me the humblest of your servants from this day forth. If you fancy any little relish...\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e4",
      "predicate": "said to",
      "target": "e1",
      "evidence": "\"Oh, come!\" said the squirrel, who felt rather crusty, perhaps, because he had not seen the fun, and so did not care for the fine speeches, \"stop bowing and scraping to each other, you two...\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e4",
      "predicate": "requested",
      "target": "e1",
      "evidence": "\"Pick up the kettle, will you, <DW53>? Look! the water is running all over the floor.\""
    },
